{"id":"s4.3.4","slug":"sum-of-squares-of-fibonacci-sequence","title":"Sum of the Squares of Arbitrary Fibonacci Sequence","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">To find the sum of the squares of the first $n$ terms of an Arbitrary Fibonacci Sequence ($A_1^2 + A_2^2 + \\dots + A_n^2$), the formula is:</p><p class=\"text-center font-bold mb-4\">Sum of Squares = $A_n \\times A_{n+1} - A_1(A_2 - A_1)$</p><p class=\"mb-4\">For the Standard Fibonacci Sequence, where $A_1=1$ and $A_2=1$, the formula simplifies to $F_n \\times F_{n+1}$ because the second term becomes zero.</p><p>For example, $1^2 + 1^2 + 2^2 + \\dots + 34^2$ (the first 9 terms of the standard sequence) is $F_9 \\times F_{10} = 34 \\times 55 = 1870$.</p>","summary":"To find the sum of the squares of the first terms of an Arbitrary Fibonacci Sequence (), the formula is: Sum of Squares = For the Standard Fibonacci S","generation_guideline":"Ask for the sum of the squares of the first n terms of an Arbitrary or Standard Fibonacci Sequence.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $2^2 + 1^2 + 3^2 + 4^2 + 7^2$.","answer":"79","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","sequences"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $1^2 + 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + 5^2 + 8^2$.","answer":"104","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","sequences"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $2^2 + 3^2 + 5^2 + 8^2 + 13^2$.","answer":"271","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","sequences"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $1^2 + 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + 5^2 + 8^2 + 13^2$.","answer":"273","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","sequences"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $2^2 + 1^2 + 3^2 + 4^2 + 7^2 + 11^2$.","answer":"200","kind":"exact","tags":["arithmetic","sequences"]},{"id":6,"text":"Find the sum of the squares of the first 5 terms of the standard Fibonacci sequence.","answer":"40","kind":"exact","tags":["sequences"]},{"id":7,"text":"Find the sum of the squares of the first 6 terms of the sequence 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13.","answer":"104","kind":"exact","tags":["sequences"]},{"id":8,"text":"Find the sum of the squ